{"name":"Electric Laser Lime","hex":"#26ff2a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, produced by, operated with, or utilising electricity; electrical.","Of or relating to an electronic version of a musical instrument that has an acoustic equivalent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electricity; the electricity supply.","An electric powered version of something that was originally or is more commonly not electric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric"},{"term":"laser","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A device that produces a monochromatic, coherent beam of light.","A beam of light produced by such a device; a laser beam."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut, destroy or treat with a laser.","To throw or kick with laser-like precision."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laser"},{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laser","blocks":[{"text":"A laser is a device that emits light through a process of optical amplification based on the stimulated emission of electromagnetic radiation. The word laser originated as an acronym for light amplification by stimulated emission of radiation. The first laser was built in 1960 by Theodore Maiman at Hughes Research Laboratories, based on theoretical work by Charles H. Townes and Arthur Leonard Schawlow and the optical amplifier patented by Gordon Gould."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Guiding_the_Milky_Way_%28potw2222a%29.jpg/330p